Aim: To design and implement a watermarking technique using OpenCV to insert a watermark into an original image.
Observation:
- A watermark may consist of text, a logo, or another image.
- The watermark is blended or overlaid onto the original image.
- The watermark's transparency and position affect the visibility of the original image.
Result: A watermark was successfully inserted into the original image using OpenCV, providing a visible identification mark while retaining the main image content.
